nexoctl manages Nexo servers and any S3-compatible endpoint: aliases,
buckets, objects, sharing, anonymous access and administration.

Remote locations are written ALIAS[/BUCKET[/PREFIX]] (see "nexoctl alias");
anything else is a local path.

Usage:
  nexoctl [command]

Buckets and objects:
  cat         Print the content of objects and files
  cp          Copy files and objects
  diff        List the differences between two directories or prefixes
  du          Summarize the disk usage of prefixes and directories
  find        Find objects and files by name, size and age
  head        Print the first lines of objects and files
  ls          List buckets, objects and object versions
  mb          Make buckets
  mirror      Synchronize a directory or prefix to another one
  mv          Move files and objects
  pipe        Stream the standard input to an object
  put         Upload local files
  rb          Remove buckets
  rm          Remove objects, object versions and incomplete uploads
  stat        Show the metadata of objects, buckets and files
  tree        Show the objects and prefixes as a tree

Sharing and access:
  access      Manage the access rules of the buckets (prefix, glob, regex)
  anonymous   Manage the anonymous access of buckets and prefixes
  cache       Manage the cache of the distributions
  cors        Manage the CORS configuration of buckets
  dist        Manage the distributions: custom domains of the buckets
  presign     Generate a raw presigned URL for any method
  share       Share objects with links that need no credentials

Bucket and object settings:
  encrypt     Manage the default encryption of buckets
  event       Manage the event notifications of buckets
  ilm         Manage the lifecycle rules of buckets (expiration, noncurrent versions, uploads)
  legalhold   Manage the Object Lock legal hold of objects
  media       Manage the video rules of buckets and the media worker (Admin API)
  quota       Manage the hard quota of buckets (Admin API)
  retention   Manage the Object Lock retention of objects and buckets
  tag         Manage the tags of buckets and objects
  version     Print the nexoctl version, or manage bucket versioning

Administration:
  admin       Administer a Nexo server (Admin API)

Configuration:
  alias       Manage server aliases (saved in ~/.nexoctl/config.json)
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command

Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
  -h, --help                help for nexoctl
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)
  -v, --version             version for nexoctl

Use "nexoctl [command] --help" for more information about a command.
